  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 6, ‘Share of countries by the number of SDG 3.c.1 occupations for which stock data are available on the NHWA data platform in the last five years (2020–2024)’ (Source: WHO National Health Workforce Accounts, 2025). A 100% stacked horizontal bar chart showing the distribution across five categories (No occupation, 1 occupation, 2 occupations, 3 occupations, and All occupations — medical doctors, nursing and midwifery personnel, dentists, and pharmacists) for Global, WHO regions (AFR, AMR, SEAR, EUR, EMR, WPR), and World Bank income groups (HIC, UMIC, LMIC, LIC). Globally, 84% of countries reported stock data for all four SDG 3.c.1 occupations in 2020–2024 (6% for 3, 4% for 2, 5% for 1, and 3% for none), ranging regionally from 69% in AMR to 94% in AFR.",
